<title>PAKISTAN: KARACHI PORT HANDLES 31,124 TONNES CARGO.</title>
<headline>KARACHI PORT HANDLES 31,124 TONNES CARGO.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 31,124 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Wednesday, compared to 83,968 tonnes on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>						Wednesday	Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo			  8,184	    3,060</p>
<p>    Import cargo			  22,940	   80,908</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, four ships sailed and one berthed. In the next 24 hours, five ships are expected to sail and 11 to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at the Karachi Port: Commodity	     Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		   Berthing</p>
<p>Fuel oil		20,000	 Iliad		  14/8</p>
<p>Tallow		   6,000	 Jiang She-32	 14/8</p>
<p>Jet fuel		25,000	 Keefan		 15/8</p>
<p>Vegetable oil	 18,600	 Kristal		14/8</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom (9221) 5685192; Fax 5673428</p>
</text>
